From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:52:50 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 259/297] Meridian: explains macOS's questions first, moves
 itself into Applications, moves in from Chrome

- Before macOS asks about the camera, the microphone, the location,
  notifications or recording the screen for the first time, Meridian's
  own sheet says what will appear and which button to press (a drawing
  of it), and where to change it if the wrong one got pressed (opens that
  System Settings pane). Once per kind. --meridian-test-system-asks fakes
  macOS for tests.
- "Restart to update" from 0.x to 1.x says macOS may ask about "Meridian
  Safe Storage": press Always Allow.
- Started from Downloads (or unzipped elsewhere after downloading) it
  offers to move itself into Applications; an older Meridian there is
  replaced (to the Trash; the profile is never touched). Test switches
  point everything at temp folders.
- The welcome tour moves in from Chrome with real counts (profiles, open
  tabs, bookmarks, passwords), and lets the person pick when Arc and
  Chrome are both here; the keychain question is drawn, Allow glowing.

